    "body": "**PROCESS_VERSION 1** · PR #682 · 2026-11-10\n\nThe baseline. It brings in every process change merged so far, including today's:\n- `needs-maintainer` (yellow) review label for PRs that are read but not built (#459).\n- `P?` label: a paused issue is never picked up, claimed or re-prioritised (#552).\n- A fork syncs product code only at release tags; process files sync every session (#562, this PR).\n- The `PR-reviewer` agent sets one review label, works in `.claude/worktrees/`, and runs tests in the foreground (#508).\n- `review-prs` posts an estimated token cost when a PR turns merge-ready (#680).\n- This version mechanism (#682).\n\n**What a fork must do now:** pull the process files once by hand (the command in this issue's body). From then on, your agent checks `PROCESS_VERSION` at the start of each session and pulls future changes itself.\n\n@mkinney @austin62jake @seelesturm @tbrasselle - you're the current contributors working from forks. Please subscribe to this issue, so you're notified when the process changes.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
