    "body": "**PROCESS_VERSION 3** · PR #685 · 2026-11-10\n\n- **New project skill `/resolve-conflicts`** (`.claude/skills/resolve-conflicts/`):\n  - **Contributor mode** (`/resolve-conflicts [login]`): merges main into your conflicting PRs (never rebase or force-push), keeps both sides of additive conflicts, takes main's snapshot PNGs and changelog files, runs the targeted gate, pushes, and comments \"ready for a re-check\". If both sides changed the same logic, it stops and reports.\n  - **Maintainer mode** (`/resolve-conflicts check`): re-checks every `conflicts` PR and restores `merge-ready` or routes it to a review.\n- **AGENTS.md, Autonomous Work Law:** conflicting PRs are re-merged by their author, and the maintainer re-checks. Fork agents run contributor mode at the start of each session, after the process-file sync.\n\n**Fork action:** pull the process files (the command in this issue's body). Then run `/resolve-conflicts` on your open PRs: 18 of yesterday's merge-ready PRs now conflict with main after the latest merges.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
