    "body": "`PROCESS_VERSION 6` · PR #747 · AGENTS.md Issue Law \"Every issue is weighted by effort\":\n- **Labels:** one `effort:low|medium|high|max` label per issue, set when the issue is filed. The labels exist now.\n- **Safety floor:** G-code, collision/gouge checks, stock simulation, geometry and every P0 are at least `effort:high`.\n- **Workers:** issues are worked by `.claude/agents/issue-worker-<effort>.md` (haiku / sonnet / opus / fable) through the new `/work-issue` skill.\n- **Reviews:** they run at least on the medium tier, and on high under the safety floor.\n- **Escalation:** two failed quick gates, or work bigger than the label, raises the label one step and releases the issue. Only the maintainer lowers a label.\n- **Costs:** the `review-prs` cost comment records the effort and any escalation.\n\n**Forks:** sync process files (`git checkout upstream/main -- AGENTS.md .claude/agents .claude/skills .claude/PROCESS_VERSION scripts/gate.ps1 scripts/gate.sh`). Set an effort label on new issues. If your models differ, edit only the `model:` line in the four `issue-worker-*` agents.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "pin": null,
