    "body": "`PROCESS_VERSION 14` · PR #881 · a contributor's claim must be live. AGENTS.md \"A claim comment is a claim\" and review-prs step 4: a contributor's claim holds an issue only while there is an open PR by the claimant for it, a commit on the claimant's branch in the last 48 hours, or a comment by the claimant on the issue in the last 48 hours. Otherwise it is stale: it is not mirrored into a `claimed` label, and a label behind it is removed with a comment. A claim also ends when the claimant's last comment withdraws it, when the maintainer releases it, or when it has been released as stale - and an ended claim is never mirrored back from its old comment; only a new `claimed:` comment is a claim again. `P?` issues are never relabelled by the sweep. The 4 h rule for the owner account's own agents is unchanged. · A fork: pull the process files (the command in this issue's body). For contributors: a claim comment alone holds an issue for 48 hours; after that keep it live with an open PR, a recent commit on your branch, or a comment on the issue; renew a released claim with a new `claimed:` comment.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
