    "body": "`PROCESS_VERSION 15` · PR #913 · build cycle (#900)\n\nWhat changed:\n- `cargo xtask gate` uses **sccache** as a shared compile cache when `sccache` is on PATH (sets `RUSTC_WRAPPER` and a 20G cache cap). An existing `RUSTC_WRAPPER` or `CAMCRAFT_NO_SCCACHE=1` wins; without sccache nothing changes.\n- The dev profile is lighter: line-table debug info for our crates, none for dependencies, dependency `opt-level` 1 (was 2). The release profile is untouched. `--config profile.dev.debug=true` restores full debug info for a debugger session.\n- Skills and agents (work-issue, resolve-conflicts, PR-reviewer): do **not** export `CARGO_TARGET_DIR` as an environment variable - sccache hashes `CARGO_*` variables, so with it set there are no cache hits across worktrees. Use each worktree's default `target/`.\n\nWhat a fork must do: pull the process files (the command in this issue's body). Optional: install sccache (`cargo install sccache --locked` or your package manager) to get the shared cache. The first build after this lands rebuilds everything once (the profile changed).\n\nMeasured on Windows only (cold build 395 s -> 177 s with a warm cache, `target/` 43 % smaller). Linux and macOS are untested: #914 and #915 are open for contributors on those systems.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "pin": null,
