    "body": "`PROCESS_VERSION 16` · PR #944 · compile cache: how agents use it, and the release build stays out of it (#935)\n\nWhat changed:\n- `work-issue`, `resolve-conflicts`, the `PR-reviewer` and `gate-runner` agents, and AGENTS.md now say: prefer `cargo xtask gate ...` (it turns the compile cache on); for a direct cargo call set `RUSTC_WRAPPER=sccache` only when `sccache` is on PATH (cargo fails if the wrapper is missing); never export `CARGO_TARGET_DIR`.\n- `cargo xtask release` builds the shipped binary without a compiler wrapper even when `RUSTC_WRAPPER` or `CARGO_BUILD_RUSTC_WRAPPER` is set in the environment. The release gate tier may still use the cache.\n\nWhat a fork must do: pull the process files (the command in this issue's body). A maintainer who wants every agent on their machine to use the cache can set `RUSTC_WRAPPER=sccache` in their own, not checked-in, settings; do not put it in `.cargo/config.toml` or the checked-in `.claude/settings.json` (it breaks machines without sccache).\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "pin": null,
